<!-- Case Reassigned — Original (booted) doctor notification (P1-FIN-2) -->
<h2 style="margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:#0B6B5F;">
  Case Reassigned
</h2>

<p style="margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#4A4640;">
  Hi Dr. {{doctorName}},
</p>

<p style="margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#4A4640;">
  Case <strong>{{caseReference}}</strong> was reassigned because the SLA window expired before {{#if isAcceptanceBreach}}you accepted the case{{else}}your report was submitted{{/if}}. A different specialist will continue the case.
</p>

<!-- Payout note (Batch B 2026-09-21). NOTE: HTML comments ship in the sent
     email source, so keep them free of retired policy wording. This box
     states the payout policy plainly instead of promising money that will
     not arrive. -->
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin:24px 0;background-color:#fffaf0;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #feebc8;">
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:20px 24px;">
      <p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;color:#9a3412;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.5px;">Payment</p>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#4A4640;">
        Because the case was reassigned before your report was delivered, <strong>no fee is payable for it</strong> under Tashkheesa's payout policy.
      </p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p style="margin:24px 0 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#7A736A;line-height:1.6;">
  If you believe this was assigned in error, reply to this email and our team will look into it.
</p>

<p style="margin:16px 0 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#9A9287;line-height:1.5;">
  Repeated SLA breaches may temporarily pause your account from receiving new cases.
</p>
